B
) The protein-protein docking was performed using the ClusPro 2.0 web server. Model exhibiting the probable interaction of nsP2 (red surface, PDB ID: 3TRK) with Catenin-α-1 (green surface, PDB ID: 4IGG). (
C
)The figure highlights polar interactions (yellow bridge) between residues of nsP2 (red) and host Catenin-α-1 (green).
Fig 2
The Catenin-α-1 protein is crucial for CHIKV infection. Vero cells were mock-infected or infected with CHIKV and harvested at various time points. (
